// A remap whose target lowers to a builtin or operator expression must still
// re-derive under the remapped point. Each of these reads p directly (rather
// than through a call that takes the remapped p as its first argument), so the
// coordinate has to travel through a re-derivation helper — before the fix they
// silently ignored it and evaluated at the original p.

shift = [2, 0, 0];
n = normalize([1, 0, 1]);
pt = [0.5, 0, 0];

// builtin call target
viaBuiltin = remap(length(p), p - shift);

// operator expression over a builtin
viaExpr = remap(dot(p - pt, n), [abs(p.x), p.y, p.z]);

// a user function whose body is a remap, called directly: the body inlines to
// an operator tree that reads p, which is how the Aerospace Bracket's mirrored
// side draft (a thunk passed to unionRoundExact) lost its abs.
mirrored() { return remap(plane(pt, n), [abs(p.x), p.y, p.z]); }
viaFn = mirrored();

// for contrast: a library call threads the remapped p as its first argument
viaLib = remap(sphere(0), p - shift);

return viaBuiltin, viaExpr, viaFn, viaLib;
